{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197528",
      "title": "Working with Icons (Button Icons)",
      "lectureOrder": 69,
      "videoOrder": 66,
      "sourceHash": "520a734188c0d6fad23baa7733c7149b569e812f6df2e5567e3d9fd36886f6e3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.46,
          "en": "So now we're making good progress here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.46,
          "end": 7.89,
          "en": "We worked on these buttons, but I'm not done yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 10.67,
          "en": "There are two main things I wanna change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.67,
          "end": 13.54,
          "en": "before we move on to the Game Over screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.54,
          "end": 16.39,
          "en": "And the first thing which I'd like to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.39,
          "end": 20.24,
          "en": "is the icons in the buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.24,
          "end": 23.48,
          "en": "At the moment we have regular characters in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.48,
          "end": 27.2,
          "en": "a minus and a plus, and I would like to use proper icons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.2,
          "end": 29.23,
          "en": "which are a bit prettier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.23,
          "end": 32.76,
          "en": "In addition, I also want to use custom fonts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.76,
          "end": 36.69,
          "en": "so that I'm not stuck with these default device fonts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.69,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "which are okay but which I don't wanna use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 42.74,
          "en": "but that I instead can use my own custom fonts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.74,
          "end": 45.5,
          "en": "because of course, that is also a typical requirement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.5,
          "end": 48.44,
          "en": "that you wanna bring your own fonts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.44,
          "end": 50.92,
          "en": "Now let's start with the icons though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.92,
          "end": 53.33,
          "en": "Thankfully, when working with Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.33,
          "end": 55.64,
          "en": "adding icons is super simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.64,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "because Expo and Expo-created projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 62.42,
          "en": "already come with a library, a package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.42,
          "end": 65.29,
          "en": "that allows us to use icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.29,
          "end": 68.73,
          "en": "We just have to add a import here at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.73,
          "end": 73.73,
          "en": "and we import something from @expo/vector-icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.27,
          "end": 79.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now this should be available automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.21000000000001,
          "end": 82.46000000000001,
          "en": "out of the box without you installing anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.46000000000001,
          "end": 85.763,
          "en": "because it is a peer dependency of Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.83,
          "end": 91.83,
          "en": "And from this package, you can import various icon sets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 94.74000000000001,
          "en": "Now, if you search for Expo vector icons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 97.97,
          "en": "you should find the official icons documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.97,
          "end": 100.32,
          "en": "And there, you can learn more about this library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.32,
          "end": 102.56,
          "en": "and that it is installed by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.56,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "if you created your project with Expo in it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 106.47999999999999,
          "en": "and how you can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.47999999999999,
          "end": 109.75999999999999,
          "en": "and which kind of icon sets you can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.75999999999999,
          "end": 111.163,
          "en": "you can learn more here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 114.86,
          "en": "Now, one icon set that's built in which I like a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.86,
          "end": 116.393,
          "en": "are the Ionicons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 120.17,
          "en": "Actually, there are more icon sets available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.17,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "which provide different kinds of icons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 125.53,
          "en": "but Ionicons is one of them, which I like a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.53,
          "end": 129.67,
          "en": "Now on the official docs about Expo vector icons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.67,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "you can find a list of the built-in icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 136,
          "en": "And for example, there if you search for minus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136,
          "end": 138.82,
          "en": "you find various minuses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.82,
          "end": 140.65,
          "en": "belonging to different icon sets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.65,
          "end": 144.29,
          "en": "which are included with Expo vector icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.29,
          "end": 145.99,
          "en": "And you do, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.99,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "also find the Ionicons minus in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 152.8,
          "en": "For this, I'll add a little filter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.8,
          "end": 154.94299999999998,
          "en": "to filter only for Ionicons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 159.48,
          "en": "and actually search for remove.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 161.97,
          "en": "And then here you find various icons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 165.61,
          "en": "and I will use this md-remove icon, which is this minus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.61,
          "end": 168.27,
          "en": "But you can of course use any icon you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "This name is important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 173.2,
          "en": "because you use these icons by grabbing this icon set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.2,
          "end": 176.09,
          "en": "which is imported from Expo vector icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.09,
          "end": 180.06,
          "en": "And then in the place where you wanna use an icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 183.763,
          "en": "you render this as a component, as a self-closing component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.64,
          "end": 186.25,
          "en": "which gets a name prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.25,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "And now the name is that icon you want to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "And we even get auto-completion here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 194.35,
          "en": "And we, for example, get help and learn that md-remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.35,
          "end": 197.043,
          "en": "is indeed a valid icon we can use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 201.36,
          "en": "Now you can, in addition, also add a size prompt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 203.17000000000002,
          "en": "which sets the size in pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.17000000000002,
          "end": 206.763,
          "en": "And here I'll set this to 24 to have a nice big icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.9,
          "end": 210.73,
          "en": "And you can set the color, and here I'll set this to white,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.73,
          "end": 213.653,
          "en": "but you could also add a hex code or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 219.314,
          "en": "And with that, now we have this nice minus here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.314,
          "end": 221.72,
          "en": "And we can do the same thing for the plus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.72,
          "end": 225.51,
          "en": "We replace the plus character with Ionicons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.51,
          "end": 229.32,
          "en": "And now instead of md-remove, it's indeed md-add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.32,
          "end": 232.11,
          "en": "Same size, same color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 235.47,
          "en": "And with that added, we now also have this plus here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.47,
          "end": 238.02,
          "en": "And I'm using the same icons on both platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.02,
          "end": 241.3,
          "en": "You could even use different icons on different platforms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.3,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "but we will learn more about platform specific code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 246.223,
          "en": "in the next course section.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
